{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 3, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the sunlight unusually vibrant. He sat up in bed, a strange, almost clinical awareness washing over him. The room was…perfect. Too perfect. The floral wallpaper, the precisely arranged books on the shelf, the gentle sunlight filtering through the window – it all felt staged, like a meticulously crafted backdrop. He reached out to touch a framed photograph on the nightstand, and his fingers passed right through it. A wave of dizziness hit him, and he stumbled out of bed, noticing the uncanny smoothness of the floor, the lack of dust, the unnervingly symmetrical arrangement of everything. A notification popped into his vision, a translucent box hovering near his temple: \"Welcome to Aethelgard! Level 1: The Shirewood Residence. Objective: Commence Daily Routine.\" Panic tightened its grip. This wasn't his life. This was…a game.\n\n***\n\nHe cautiously ventured outside, the world unfolding in crisp, high-definition detail. Villagers strolled by, their movements slightly jerky, their conversations repeating phrases with unnerving regularity. A quest marker appeared above a nearby blacksmith’s shop, pulsing with a faint blue light: \"Gather 5 Iron Ingots.\" Arthur pinched himself, but the sensation felt muted, unreal. He tried to shout, to scream, but his voice sounded…processed, like a character speaking lines. He was trapped. A wave of despair threatened to engulf him, but a flicker of defiance ignited within. He wouldn't just passively accept this reality. He would learn the rules, exploit the glitches, and find a way to escape Aethelgard, even if it meant becoming the hero the game expected him to be.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.407365083694458}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00015984688070602715}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.08786557614803314}, {"token": "▁sun